  "id": "COMPOUND:31393 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "Goiazensolide appears to interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging from its interaction with Amine oxidase [flavin-containing] B, which in turn targets the kinase. This suggests a potential role for Goiazensolide in modulating the activity of this kinase through its interaction with an enzyme involved in metabolic pathways. Additionally, Goiazensolide is also shown to target Protein kinase C eta, which is a known regulator of the CDC2L1 kinase. While the exact mechanism by which Goiazensolide influences the activity of CDC2L1 remains unclear, the presence of multiple targets in the same kinase family suggests a possible mechanism involving the regulation of kinase activity through the interaction with different kinases. The evidence supports a potential role for Goiazensolide in modulating the activity of the CDC2L1 kinase, possibly through the regulation of its upstream targets.",
